          "classification": "revision-recommended",
          "evidence": "ASM-09 fixes initial session and readiness but TYPE-08 also exposes rearm, notice, six fault bits, and aggregate fault; PASS-02 forbids any unconstrained CTRL-02 member, and those stateless owner facts do not exist before the first complete evaluation.",
          "requested_change": "Amend ASM-09 and PART-14 initialization to set CTRL-02 exactly to Off, startReady=false, sustainReady=false, rearm=Blocked, notice=Off, vector=[false,false,false,false,false,false], anyFault=false; retain initial CTRL-01 Inhibit/Isolate/Apply. Change no PART, INT, metric, scenario, policy, or claim-boundary exclusion."
        },
        {
          "classification": "revision-recommended",
          "evidence": "PART-11 preserves/bundles six assigned fault inputs before deriving their OR, and PART-14 copies session/readiness/rearm/vector/OR before deriving notice. Under M-17 those copied fields cannot support owner-local-fact or semantic-usage credit, although six-input OR and prioritized notice selection make both usages substantive.",
          "requested_change": "Narrow DS-OWN-02, DS-FAULT-01/02, PART-11, PART-14, AUD-PAD-01, and later ownership-audit claims so PART-11 is credited only for anyFault derivation and PART-14 only for notice classification; retain vector/status preservation as uncredited coherence obligations. Keep all PARTs, INT-25 and INT-29..35, counts, outputs, and domain behavior unchanged."
        },
        {
          "classification": "no-concern",
          "evidence": "Extensionally, PART-01..05 collapse invalid alternatives or derive multi-class applicability; PART-06/07/10/12 make prior-state-dependent choices; PART-08/09/13 combine inputs into nonbijective decisions. None requires identity behavior for owner credit.",
          "requested_change": ""
        },
        {
          "classification": "localized-mapping",
          "evidence": "The 35-INT owner graph is acyclic with state local to PART-06/07/10/12. Trusted Isolette GUMBO forms and a fresh Sireum v4.20260630.386eac9f check against library commit 9016cbcceefa92f0068e1811923704dd261d15f1 support typed record ports, local state, compute_cases, same-owner next-state outputs, System/Process/Thread containment, and direct fan-out; the check exited 0 with Well-formed!.",
          "requested_change": ""
        },
        {
          "classification": "no-concern",
          "evidence": "The complete boundary/prior-state product is 5,529,600 valuations. The 29 counted cases can remain exactly four owner-local compute-case partitions, with qualification/composition equations uncounted, while a factorized analyzer checks the same local relations plus multi-step fresh-request and recovery traces under the retained watchdog.",
          "requested_change": ""
        }
